<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Sections 1 and 2 shall commence on the date of
assent to this Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.2-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_82141c57-305a-4bf0-8714-8dc16a332fb6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.2-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Except as provided by subsection (1), this Act
shall commence on such day as may be appointed by the Governor and notified by
proclamation published in the Gazette.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_04c12d98-8491-47f8-84d0-8089b6706861"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>3</no><heading guid="_9f595d0e-0525-4ff9-b1ea-1b6ca11e9a74"
id="sec.3-he"><b>Definitions</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_a429765e-dda8-4370-ad13-76801231ef22"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this Act, except in so far as the context or
subject-matter otherwise indicates or requires:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_3d6531a2-0f16-4e62-990f-7781808906a4"
id="sec.3-def.appliedprovision"><b><i>applied provision</i></b></defterm>
means a provision of:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_97a29311-fb0b-469a-81f3-0ec4288eea20" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Insurance Contracts Act
1984</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_40a30fad-fa54-4d7e-81fe-c4efb754dc2d" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.b"
status="repealed">
<no>(b)</no>
<repealed><repealedtxt></repealedtxt></repealed>
</li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_88c249a9-b57f-4286-9b42-c2ecaa8b1975" id="sec.3-ssec.1-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">an instrument in force under either of those
Acts,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">being a provision that, pursuant to this Act, applies as
a law of New South Wales.</txt></block>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_e8d0aa01-94b3-4786-aee4-f0777d35e26f"
id="sec.3-def.regulation"><b><i>regulation</i></b></defterm> means a
regulation made under this Act.</txt></block></deflist>
</block></tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_6229072c-efde-44b3-9ba2-5e89e45a2f65"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">An applied provision shall be construed in
accordance with the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Acts Interpretation Act 1901</i></name></legref> of the
Commonwealth, as in force from time to time.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c074b6c8-7101-4caf-9bec-d81657933fab"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Without affecting the generality of section 31 of
the <legref refid="act-1987-015" jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Interpretation Act 1987</i></name></legref>, this Act shall
be construed as operating to the full extent of, but so as not to exceed, the
legislative power of Parliament.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.3-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f5ab117b-3740-44de-8bd1-31fa28dfd9bf"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.3-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Notes included in this Act do not form part of
this Act.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 3:</b> Am 1987 No 48,
Sch 32; 2002 No 26, Sch 2.5 [1]&#8211;[3].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_57e059f3-015c-42e2-85a1-4caf67a6e18f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>4</no><heading guid="_f1678618-9df4-4c3d-824e-cc0b54e36f83"
id="sec.4-he"><b>Crown bound</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_fd3124fd-5120-4e04-9c7e-08d1fb0e1ecf"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This Act and the applied provisions bind the
Crown in right of New South Wales and also, so far as the legislative power of
Parliament permits, the Crown in all its other
capacities.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.4-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3250d2a1-92c3-4a6b-a272-7129101b714e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.4-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Nothing in this Act renders the Crown, whether in
right of New South Wales or otherwise, liable to be prosecuted for an offence
against an applied provision.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.5">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c2400a0a-8680-47f6-a450-83a32bccfde4"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>5</no><heading guid="_e9dd6d6d-0617-4e50-af57-20b5aed6389b"
id="sec.5-he"><b>Application of <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Insurance Contracts Act
1984</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth etc</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_0db7d616-340b-4f16-ac49-2a560d418452"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Except to the extent to which the regulations
otherwise provide and subject to any modifications specified in the
regulations, the provisions of:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_894a3575-5748-4121-9024-edc20481b521" id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Insurance Contracts Act
1984</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth, as in force from time to time,
and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_213807ae-ea90-4b94-8c2c-340095392094" id="sec.5-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">any instrument in force under that
Act,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">apply as laws of New South Wales to and in respect of
all contracts of insurance and proposed contracts of insurance entered into,
or proposed to be entered into, in the course of State insurance, including
contracts and proposed contracts entered into, or proposed to be entered into,
by the State and some other insurer as joint insurers.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.5-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_96af43fa-c743-47fa-9846-2d454ffbefb0"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.5-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Subsection (1) does not operate so as to apply
section 5 or 9 (2) of the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Insurance Contracts Act
1984</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth as a law of New South
Wales.</txt></block></tier>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.6">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_48a8f36b-249e-42ad-8fce-8b94108b0ad8"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>6</no><heading guid="_fb23a472-0f49-4e0b-bbd1-d0ecc8a1af16"
id="sec.6-he"><b>Application of Corporations legislation to State insurance
matters</b></heading></head>

<pre type="auto-inserted">

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e23a617d-e416-418b-bb60-8673df7b5e4d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The regulations may declare any State insurance
matter to be an applied Corporations legislation matter for the purposes of
Part 3 of the <legref refid="act-2001-032" jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Corporations (Ancillary Provisions)
Act 2001</i></name></legref> (with such modifications as may be specified in
the declaration) in relation to the following:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_299d3331-307a-4555-b2f4-a69e6e92f2a7" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">all or any of the provisions of Chapter 7
(Financial services and markets) of the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Corporations Act
2001</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_b908f8f5-37e4-4522-8818-af736d9bf0a4" id="sec.6-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">all or any of the provisions of the <legref
jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Australian
Securities and Investments Commission Act 2001</i></name></legref> of the
Commonwealth relating to financial products or financial
markets.</txt></block></li></list>
</block>
<note type="legtext" guid="_31c09c35-e7cf-4748-8643-31b09e5a2b29"
id="sec.6-ssec.1-note"><heading guid="_4950372d-2fda-4530-9044-e0e74feee725"
id="sec.6-ssec.1-note-he"><b>Note&#8212;</b></heading>
<block><txt break.before="1">Part 3 of the <legref refid="act-2001-032"
jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Corporations
(Ancillary Provisions) Act 2001</i></name></legref> provides for the
application of provisions of the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Corporations Act
2001</i></name></legref> and Part 3 of the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Australian Securities and Investments
Commission Act 2001</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth as laws of the
State in respect of any matter declared by a law of the State (whether with or
without modification) to be an applied Corporations legislation matter for the
purposes of that Part in relation to those Commonwealth provisions. Section 14
(2) of the <legref refid="act-2001-032" jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Corporations (Ancillary Provisions)
Act 2001</i></name></legref> ensures that a declaration made for the purposes
of Part 3 of that Act only operates to apply a provision of the Corporations
legislation to a matter as a law of the State if that provision does not
already apply to the matter as a law of the Commonwealth. If a provision
referred to in a declaration already applies as a law of the Commonwealth,
nothing in the declaration will affect its continued operation as a law of the
Commonwealth.</txt></block></note>
</tier>
</pre>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_3cf3adc1-0733-410e-a8c2-2e246c6a176f"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Without limiting subsection (1), any such
regulations may:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_1dd56fa0-cf17-4da4-87c7-3d6034de453e" id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">specify modifications to the definitions and
other interpretative provisions of the Corporations legislation relevant to
any provision of the Commonwealth legislation that is the subject of the
declaration, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_0e6cfb6c-cf0d-4b41-adfe-f0b3f74fa083" id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">provide for ASIC to exercise a function under any
provision of the Corporations legislation that is the subject of the
declaration, but only if:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_0b41e853-725b-49f1-91c5-2c81b5fa3b49"
id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.b-para2.i">
<no>(i)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">ASIC is to exercise that function pursuant to an
agreement of the kind referred to in section 11 (8) or (9A) (b) of the <legref
jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Australian
Securities and Investments Commission Act 2001</i></name></legref> of the
Commonwealth, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_889f37ec-bc17-4bae-90db-5ab77b91872a"
id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.b-para2.ii">
<no>(ii)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">ASIC is authorised to exercise that function
under section 11 of the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="yes"><i>Australian Securities and Investments Commission Act
2001</i></name></legref> of the Commonwealth, and</txt></block></li></list>
</block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_62e716f1-8e15-4405-a4fb-6cfbef4fae42" id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">specify that a reference to ASIC in any provision
of the Corporations legislation that is the subject of the declaration is to
be read as a reference to another person, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_ac99b7ca-3327-4639-863d-6ee909cb83d6" id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.d">
<no>(d)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">identify the provisions of the Corporations
legislation to which the declaration relates by reference to that legislation
as in force at a particular time, and</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_d6735515-96f2-4f69-8d64-fd34b152f74e" id="sec.6-ssec.2-para1.e">
<no>(e)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">specify a court of this State (other than the
Supreme Court) to exercise any function conferred on a court or the Court by
any provision of the Corporations legislation to which the declaration
relates.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_f5a0bdf9-5feb-432d-bbe3-bc162df6d615"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Words and expressions used in this section and
also in Part 3 of the <legref refid="act-2001-032" jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Corporations (Ancillary Provisions)
Act 2001</i></name></legref> have the same meanings as they have in that
Part.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.6-ssec.4">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b352a1e2-e285-4dcb-b480-7de41c41a12b"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.6-ssec.4"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(4)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">In this section:</txt>
<deflist>
<block><txt break.before="1"><defterm type="definition"
guid="_28748f8b-e88c-469d-8e15-88c04b4d2288"
id="sec.6-def.Stateinsurancematter"><b><i>State insurance
matter</i></b></defterm> means:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_b55aedb2-b675-45cd-ba01-71b43fff84e6" id="sec.6-ssec.4-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">State insurance within the meaning of section 51
(xiv) of the <legref jurisd="CTH" type="act" check="unknown"><name
emphasis="no">Commonwealth Constitution</name></legref>,
or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_46f5d7db-f4df-415e-86bc-a9f08feea497" id="sec.6-ssec.4-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">contracts of insurance and proposed contracts of
insurance entered into, or proposed to be entered into, by the State and some
other insurer as joint insurers, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_c921b527-4bba-470b-9ae9-288a09569d95" id="sec.6-ssec.4-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">conduct in connection with contracts and proposed
contracts of the kind referred to in paragraph (b).</txt></block></li></list>
</block></deflist>
</block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 6:</b> Subst 2002 No
26, Sch 2.5 [4].</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.7">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_615dbe85-26b8-4ad4-8a80-f2a0b586b91a"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>7</no><heading guid="_2ee50266-d1a2-492c-8a91-5730c58abe07"
id="sec.7-he"><b>Exclusion of GIO insurance funds administration
business</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_e04bad9b-d339-4f03-820d-d4d847e51737"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The applied provisions do not apply to or in
respect of the insurance funds administration business of the Government
Insurance Office of New South Wales (that is, business of the kind referred to
in section 5B (1) (b) of the <legref jurisd="NSW" type="act"
check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Government Insurance Act
1927</i></name></legref>) or to or in respect of that Office in its conduct of
that business.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.7-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7c8bc5b3-8743-4716-9e81-46f2d44988a0"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.7-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">This section continues to have effect with
respect to that insurance funds administration business even though it is
transferred to another person or body under the <legref refid="act-1991-038"
jurisd="NSW" type="act" check="unknown"><name emphasis="yes"><i>Government
Insurance Office (Privatisation) Act
1991</i></name></legref>.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 7:</b> Am 1991 No 38,
Sch 2.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.8">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_321a91ec-a07b-434b-8a62-a892a38454fd"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>8</no><heading guid="_8d063973-4112-4189-8f7c-2d2d6bac6cef"
id="sec.8-he"><b>Recovery of penalties</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_c43d6b04-33d8-49fb-8a07-b9beefc2f981"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Proceedings for an offence against an applied
provision may be dealt with summarily:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_2ecf4f72-27e9-4f87-a0de-6adeb92e5fae" id="sec.8-ssec.1-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">before the Local Court, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_c30c2a55-5067-4f53-a82d-9e9dd02c9ca7" id="sec.8-ssec.1-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">before the Supreme Court in its summary
jurisdiction.</txt></block></li></list>
</block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_59c7868d-0953-4238-8e21-d7118385e899"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Where proceedings for an offence against an
applied provision are dealt with before the Local Court, the maximum pecuniary
penalty that may be imposed in respect of the offence is $5,000 or the
pecuniary penalty indicated in the provision in respect of the offence,
whichever is the lesser.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.8-ssec.3">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_b1f20a31-66c0-4df3-a2b0-70db5da14e1e"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.8-ssec.3"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(3)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">Where proceedings for an offence against an
applied provision are dealt with before the Supreme Court in its summary
jurisdiction, the maximum pecuniary penalty that may be imposed in respect of
the offence is the pecuniary penalty indicated in the provision in respect of
the offence.</txt></block></tier>


<content type="historynote"><txt break.before="1"><b>s 8:</b> Am 2007 No 94,
Sch 5.</txt></content>
</level>


<level type="clause" id="sec.9">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="spent.amends" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_208477bb-0643-44df-ba8d-b91bfc286763"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>9</no><heading guid="_fe2b2dc2-3bbc-4d19-be02-9743426e8947"
id="sec.9-he"><b>Regulations</b></heading></head>

<tier type="subclause" id="sec.9-ssec.1">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_9da2f905-29b9-4fde-b857-d10a1c2e54e6"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9-ssec.1"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(1)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">The Governor may make regulations, not
inconsistent with this Act, for or with respect to any matter that by this Act
is required or permitted to be prescribed or that is necessary or convenient
to be prescribed for carrying out or giving effect to this
Act.</txt></block></tier>


<tier type="subclause" id="sec.9-ssec.2">
<parentattributes>
<attrib name="affected.by.uncommenced" value="0"></attrib>
<attrib name="provision.type" value="other"></attrib>
<attrib name="guid" value="_7837b897-28b5-4668-a239-3402ca2ee42d"></attrib>
<attrib name="id" value="sec.9-ssec.2"></attrib></parentattributes>

<head>
<no>(2)</no></head>
<block><txt break.before="1">A provision of a regulation may:</txt>
<list number.type="default" unnumbered.indent="0">
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_cda0d6f8-f196-4ca9-849c-9b2e4bead86a" id="sec.9-ssec.2-para1.a">
<no>(a)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">apply generally or be limited in its application
by reference to specified exceptions or factors,</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_b69ad925-9821-42bc-8797-092f3b70ba10" id="sec.9-ssec.2-para1.b">
<no>(b)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">apply differently according to different factors
of a specified kind, or</txt></block></li>
<li provision.type="other" affected.by.uncommenced="0"
guid="_3605f104-4b12-4647-8513-2567342dcd1c" id="sec.9-ssec.2-para1.c">
<no>(c)</no>
<block><txt break.before="1">authorise any matter or thing to be from time to
time determined, applied or regulated by any specified person or
body,</txt></block></li></list>

<txt break.before="1">or may do any combination of those
things.</txt></block></tier>
</level>
</content>


